---
export const prerender = true;

const effectiveDate = '26 November 2026';
const appName = 'Tsundoku';
const domainHost = 'tsundoku.singbaobao.com';
const contactEmail = 'privacy@beetlskills.com';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Privacy Policy — {appName}</title>
    <style>
      :root {
        color-scheme: light dark;
        --bg: #fafafa;
        --surface: #ffffff;
        --text: #18181b;
        --muted: #52525b;
        --border: #e4e4e7;
        --accent: #0f766e;
      }

      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root {
          --bg: #09090b;
          --surface: #111114;
          --text: #f4f4f5;
          --muted: #a1a1aa;
          --border: #27272a;
          --accent: #2dd4bf;
        }
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
        line-height: 1.65;
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--text);
      }

      main {
        max-width: 780px;
        margin: 3rem auto;
        padding: 2.25rem;
        background: var(--surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 10px;
      }

      h1 {
        margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
        font-size: 1.85rem;
        line-height: 1.25;
      }

      .meta {
        margin: 0 0 2rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.92rem;
      }

      h2 {
        margin: 2rem 0 0.65rem;
        font-size: 1.15rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
        padding-bottom: 0.35rem;
      }

      p,
      ul {
        margin: 0.6rem 0;
      }

      ul {
        padding-left: 1.4rem;
      }

      li + li {
        margin-top: 0.35rem;
      }

      a {
        color: var(--accent);
        text-underline-offset: 2px;
      }

      footer {
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        padding-top: 1.25rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.9rem;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta">
        Application: <strong>{appName}</strong> ({domainHost}) &middot; Effective Date: {effectiveDate}
      </p>

      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>{appName}</strong> collects, uses, stores, and
        protects information when you use the web application hosted at{' '}
        <a href={`https://${domainHost}`}>https://{domainHost}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Data We Access and Collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Account &amp; Authentication Data:</strong> When you sign in, we receive basic
          account details (such as your name, email address, and profile identifier) needed to
          maintain your session and link your shelf configuration.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Drive &amp; Google Sheets Data:</strong> With your explicit authorization via
          Google OAuth and Google Picker, {appName} accesses only the Google Sheets files you
          select or create for managing book shelves (such as reading/writing shelf rows and reading
          spreadsheet titles). We do not request blanket access to unrelated files in your Google
          Drive.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Barcode &amp; Book Lookup Inputs:</strong> ISBNs scanned or entered in the app are
          sent to book metadata services to resolve bibliographic details (such as title, authors,
          publisher, and publication year).
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Authenticate your session and associate your account with your chosen spreadsheet.</li>
        <li>Read, add, update, or remove book entries in your linked Google Sheet at your direction.</li>
        <li>Display shared shelf data when a shelf owner explicitly marks a shelf as shared.</li>
        <li>Maintain application reliability, security, and error diagnostics.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal data, run third-party advertising networks, or use Google user data
        for advertising or unrelated profiling.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Storage, Security, and Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>
        {appName} runs on Cloudflare infrastructure. Shelf settings and encrypted OAuth refresh
        tokens are stored in Cloudflare D1, while short-lived caching may use Cloudflare KV when
        configured. Sensitive tokens are encrypted prior to storage using authenticated encryption.
      </p>
      <p>
        Interactions with Google services are governed by the{' '}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Google Privacy Policy
        </a>
        .
      </p>

      <h2>4. Data Retention, Revocation, and Deletion</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Your shelf entries remain in your own Google Sheet unless you modify or delete them.
        </li>
        <li>
          You can revoke {appName}&apos;s access to your Google Account at any time via your{' '}
          <a
            href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Google Account permissions page
          </a>
          .
        </li>
        <li>
          To request deletion of account records or stored shelf configuration data associated with
          your account, contact us using the address below.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about this Privacy Policy or data removal requests, contact{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <footer>
        <a href="/">Back to {appName}</a>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>